[E-MUTUAL-SIGNATURE] Error: `f`'s type mentions `g`, which is defined together with it
   ╭─[ soundness/mutual-signature.sw:7:19 ]
   │
 7 │ def f (n : Nat) : g n = g n := rfl
   │                   ┬  
   │                   ╰── `g` is used here, in `f`'s type
   │ 
 9 │ def g : Nat -> Nat
   │     ┬  
   │     ╰── `g` is defined here
   │ 
   │ Note 1: they're checked together because `g` uses `f`
   │ 
   │ Note 2: a definition's type can only mention definitions that are finished before it, and definitions that call each other are finished together; move what the type needs out of the cycle
